%N A397781 Number of P-partitions of n where P is the labeled poset defined by a covers b if A360010(a) > A360010(b).
%C A397781 The structure of P is shown below:
%C A397781      ...
%C A397781  5 6 7 8 9 10
%C A397781     2 3 4
%C A397781       1
%C A397781 Every element in P covers all elements in the row beneath it and is covered by all elements in the row above. Specifically the partitions counted here are p-partitions over some order ideal of P. Because P is similar to the 3-d integer lattice but with additional covering relations these partitions can be represented as restricted solid partitions as shown in the example.
%H A397781 John Tyler Rascoe, <a href="/A397781/a397781.txt">PARI code</a>.
%F A397781 a(n) <= A000293(n).
%e A397781 a(3) = 7 with the number of valid arrangements of the parts shown in {}: (3){1}, (2,1){3}, (1,1,1){3}.
